// Package marks declares the marks that say what the compiler knows about a
// declaration: `builtin`, which names the IR construct a declaration
// dispatches to, and `intrinsic`, which names the native implementation that
// may replace a function's body.
//
// Unlike a user-facing mark such as `#[platforms.wildcard]` these annotate the library
// source itself: the checker reads them off a declaration as it registers it.
//
// The path is `sngl:internal/marks` and not `.../builtin`: `sngl:builtin`
// is the ambient package of built-in types, a different thing one letter away
// at the import line.
